  "note": "The temporal particle has its own consonants and is separate from אוּת, hyssop and the name Ezbai filed nearby. The Aramaic and Syriac temporal adverbs have expanded forms. Lane’s example refers to past time, while Hebrew also uses אָז of what is to come."
